-- chem/bondsep.hypercubical — the bond's two nuclei placements separated rigorously at a sample coupling, past the
-- perturbative range of chem/h2plus-net.hypercubical. The opposite placement's level is the least root of p_f and the
-- sharing placement's is at most the least root of p_n (chem/bondpoly.hypercubical, chem/h2plus-net's `hp-bond-range`),
-- in x = 280·(E − E_nucleus)/L, with s = (280 t/L)²:
--   p_f(x) = x³ − 258x² + (16520 − 6s)x + 280s,   p_n(x) = x³ − 216x² + (11264 − 3s)x + 344s.
-- Each has p′ > 0 for every x below its least root (p′ is an upward parabola whose axis, 86 and 72, is positive, and
-- p′ at the bracket point is positive), so the least root is the single crossing and is pinned by two integer
-- evaluations of opposite sign. At s = 784 (t/L = 1/10): p_f(−18) < 0 with p_f′(−18) > 0, so the opposite level
-- exceeds −18; p_n(−20) < 0 < p_n(−19) with p_n′(−19) > 0, so the sharing level is below −19. Hence at this coupling
-- the sharing placement lies strictly lower than the opposite by more than one unit of 280·E/L (`bs-784`) — a
-- non-perturbative certificate, exact in integers, where `hp-bond-range` gave only the second-order trend up to
-- s = 1156. A leaf: no module imports it.
import "charge.hypercubical"

